<Layout title="Privacy policy of this Irish salary calculator 2026" description="Nothing you enter leaves your browser: what is measured, what is not, which cookies exist, and how to exercise the rights you hold over any of that data.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-8 prose prose-slate">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <h2>Data Processing</h2>
    <p>All salary calculations are performed client-side in your browser. No personal data (salary, tax status) is collected, transmitted, or stored.</p>
    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>The calculator sets no cookies and the site carries no advertising. Microsoft Clarity, which loads when the page opens with no consent banner, sets the cookies <code>_clck</code> (one year) and <code>_clsk</code> (one day), and Microsoft may set <code>MUID</code> and <code>CLID</code> on its own domains. To refuse them, block third-party cookies or the domain clarity.ms in your browser, and clear site data to remove cookies already set; the calculator works without them.</p>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>We use Plausible Analytics, a privacy-respecting analytics tool that sets no cookies and counts page views without identifying visitors.</p>
    <p>We also use Microsoft Clarity to see how pages are used, on the basis of our legitimate interest in understanding how the site is used (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR); the site shows no consent banner. It records clicks, scrolling, pages viewed and their address, device and browser type, and an approximate location derived from the IP address. What you type into a field is masked in your browser and is not sent. Session recordings are kept for 30 days and aggregated data for up to 13 months. Microsoft may process this data in the United States, under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework and the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses; see <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft’s privacy statement</a>.</p>
    <h2>Your Rights</h2>
    <p>Under GDPR, you have rights of access, rectification, erasure and objection. The calculator itself collects no personal data. You may also lodge a complaint with the Data Protection Commission in Ireland, or with the CNIL in France, where the publisher is established.</p>
